  "live_records": {
    "q-276847": {
      "dom_id": "step-q276847",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Rationalize the denominator of the following expression:\n\n| ${p}^{2}\\sqrt{36}$ | __ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $2\\sqrt{3s}$ | __ | $s$ |",
      "worked_solution": "We must remove the radical $\\sqrt{3s}$ from the denominator. To do this, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{3s},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{p}^{2}\\sqrt{36}}{2\\sqrt{3s}} & = \\\\ \\frac{{p}^{2}\\sqrt{36}}{2\\sqrt{3s}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3s}}{\\sqrt{3s}} & = \\\\ \\frac{6{p}^{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{3s}}{2\\sqrt{3s}\\cdot \\sqrt{3s}} & = \\\\ \\frac{6{p}^{2}\\sqrt{3s}}{2{(\\sqrt{3s})}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{6{p}^{2}\\sqrt{3s}}{2\\cdot 3s} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{6}{p}^{2}\\sqrt{3s}}{\\cancel{6}s} & = \\\\ \\frac{{p}^{2}\\sqrt{3s}}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
