    "q-277015": {
      "dom_id": "step-q277015",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Rationalize the denominator of the following expression:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td width=\"80\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\" align=\"center\">$\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{x+2}}\\,=\\,$</td>\n<td width=\"80\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">{{field-1}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"60\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"60\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">$x+2$</td>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "First, we apply the quotient rule and put the numerator and denominator under separate radicals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{x+2}} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{x+2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo remove the radical $\\sqrt{x+2}$ from the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{x+2}$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{x+2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{x+2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{x+2}}{\\sqrt{x+2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{x+2}}{\\sqrt{x+2}\\cdot \\sqrt{x+2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{5(x+2)}}{(\\sqrt{x+2})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{5(x+2)}}{x+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "freeResponseTextbox-1",
