    "q-365110": {
      "dom_id": "step-q365110",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Express $\\frac{\\sqrt{m-n}}{\\sqrt{m+n}}\\,$ without radicals in the denominator.",
      "worked_solution": "To remove the radical $\\sqrt{m+n}$ from the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{m+n}$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{m-n}}{\\sqrt{m+n}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{m-n}}{\\sqrt{m+n}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{m+n}}{\\sqrt{m+n}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{m-n}\\cdot \\sqrt{m+n}}{(\\sqrt{m+n})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{(m-n)(m+n)}}{m+n} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{{m}^{2}-{n}^{2}}}{m+n}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
